# Stryker sandboxes: full copies of the repo. Left behind, vitest discovers them and
# runs every test twice, and the mutation harness reads doubled counts.
.stryker-tmp/

# Generated run output. reports/mutation/ IS tracked - these are not.
reports/vectors-node.json
reports/vectors-hermes.json
reports/sms-segments.json

# Private keys never belong in a repository, ignored or not - the EC2 key
# for the Mumbai instance was found sitting in AWS/ on 2026-10-11 and moved
# to ../swafto-keys/. These patterns are belt and braces: check:secrets
# walks the FILESYSTEM and does not read this file, so it will still fail
# on a key left in the tree. That is deliberate - a key in the working
# directory is one zip, rsync or `git add -f` away from being published.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
AWS/
